# Building Cooked UI

Before writing or changing any screen or component:

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `design/README.md` and `design/system/README.md`.
2. Find the screen in `design/screens/README.md`. Open its screenshot in `design/screens/screenshots/` and its prototype in `design/screens/prototypes/`.
3. Check the finished UI against `design/system/avoid-the-ai-look.md`. Anything on that list means it isn't done.

## Rules

- Every color, font, size, space, radius and shadow comes from `@/theme` (generated from `design/system/tokens.json` by `npm run tokens`). Never hard-code a hex value, font name or font size in a component.
- Use `Text` from `@/components/Text` with a `variant` and `color` token, and `Icon` from `@/components/Icon`.
- Fonts: Alumni Sans only for screen titles (700) and section headings (600, no underline), always 24px or bigger. Albert Sans for everything else. Caveat only on sticky notes.
- One sage (`sage`) button per screen. Every other button is a grey `surface-sunken` pill or a `sage-ink` text link.
- Bronze (`bronze`, `bronze-ink`) only marks food to use soon. Never use it for buttons, links or progress.
- Destructive actions are `error-ink` text buttons, never filled.
- No black buttons, black cards or a black tab island.
- Lists are flat rows with `line-soft` dividers, not cards.
- Tap targets are at least 44pt, even when the drawn control is smaller.
- Use only the 20 icons in `design/system/icons/`.
- Use the system keyboard, share sheet, camera and Sign in with Apple. The prototypes fake these.
- Copy comes from the prototype. Don't rewrite it or invent new copy without asking.
- Build only what the prototype shows. If something is missing (a state, an edge case), make the smallest choice that fits the design system and log it in `Decisions.md`.
- Where design files disagree, `design/system/README.md` and `design/system/tokens.json` win. See "Where the files disagree" in `design/README.md`.
